cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Molecular Simulation of Doravirine Resistance in HIV-1 Reverse Transcriptase
message: If you use this software or its derived data, please cite the paper.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Rohit
    family-names: Satija
    affiliation: Division of Infectious Diseases, Stanford University School of Medicine
  - given-names: Kaiming
    family-names: Tao
    affiliation: Division of Infectious Diseases, Stanford University School of Medicine
  - given-names: Robert W.
    family-names: Shafer
    affiliation: Division of Infectious Diseases, Stanford University School of Medicine
repository-code: https://github.com/rohitium/nnrti-mechanisms
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  All-atom explicit-solvent molecular dynamics, non-equilibrium alchemical free
  energy perturbation and MM/GBSA analysis of wild-type HIV-1 reverse
  transcriptase and 18 doravirine-associated genotypes, compared against
  measured phenotypic susceptibility.
keywords:
  - HIV-1 reverse transcriptase
  - doravirine
  - drug resistance
  - free energy perturbation
  - molecular dynamics
